# Handyman recs

- Truck language is **Send $ask**, **Look first: {named check}**, or **Pass**. Never tell a tech "Review at $185" or "conservative hours."
- **Ask** can include this week's pace. **Walk-away** is min job / margin / profit / labor only — no week pace.
- Do not Pass a clear job that still fits remaining hours just because Friday is tight. Send the week-ask.
- Look first only when we can name what to check (water, substrate, structural, photos).
- Week clock is live from this Monday–Sunday. Completed jobs use `completed_at` (else `created_at`). Scheduled / in_progress / approved always count. Quoted / needs_review do not.
- Monday / midweek / Friday exist only in `npm run sim`. App code never special-cases weekday names.
- Demo and real accounts share the same code. Mason refresh SQL is `supabase/refresh-mason-production.sql` (that business_id only).
- After engine tunes: `npm run sim` then regenerate seed SQL with `npx tsx supabase/generate-seed-sql.ts`.
- Rec misses must land on `owner_decisions.reason_code`. Pass they take, Send they decline, and Look first they close all ask why. Small price moves log too-high / too-low from direction.
- Weekly miss write-up: `npm run tune-report`. Scheduled function `weekly-tuning-report` (Mondays). Tune from the report — do not invent hours.
